A||||13||Black88GT||2 in one night....||||12||
Z||000000||Black88GT||06-06-2001||08:38 PM||||I guess since the weather is nicer now everyone is in the racing mood (including me).  <P>Some of you may remember the Eclipse turbo I raced, well this was on the same street.  I sware this street is absolutely perfect for racing.  Not much traffic, no merge lanes or anything, no kids, never any cops, perfect.<P>So anyway, the first one is on the way to work.  I see the back of a Civic Si, yellow with a body kit and exhaust.  I was so happy to see I would be pulling right up along side of him at the red light heading to the road.  Well as I pulled up, I noticed the front of his car was still electron blue!  LOL, he just got the back body kit done in yellow and the front is still stock blue.  So I looked at him and started laughing.  He must have seen me even though he had dark tinted windows, so he started revving like crazy and inching forward.  So I revved a little too.  Light turns green he barely peels (stock motor probably, or he doesnt know how to drive it) and we were side by side for about 20 feet.  I shifted into second and started pulling away, by third I was a good 4 car lengths ahead, and at 4th I we stayed even to about 110 mph then I shut it down.  At the next red light (going into residential now so no racing) he told me he has had some motor problems and look for him in about a week when he straightened them out, I was like yeah ooook and drove off.<P>Next race, coming home from work, I was coming up in the far right lane passing the rows of cars in the middle and far left lanes.  I see some guy swerve out of the row and come into my lane, behind me.  I wasn't going that fast, about 60 everyone else about 50.  But I look in my rear view and I see this mid-90s Grand Prix's right on my butt.  So I down shifted into 4th and nailed it, he was staying pretty close I was only pulling a little at first, but after about 90 (still in 4th) I was pulling away, I shifted into 5th after this turn, he couldnt go that fast around this turn so I was a good 10 car lengths ahead.  At the light he gave me a thumbs up and said he always wanted a Fiero but he didn't think they were too fast.  He felt better when I told him mine wasn't stock.<P>So thats it for tonight, probably have more Fri. night.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff (AOL IM - FieroTT)<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">     <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I><BR><I>"The Customer Can Have Any Color He Wants So Long As It's Black" </I> -Henry Ford||||reg||12
