Z||000007||Seanh||06-07-2001||12:46 AM||||I brutally exicuited a beretta last night. It was rather funny. It was on a 3 lane road, me in the right, grand prix in the middle, and beretta in left. I have a 4spd. auto on a 3.4L pushrod, so I just floored it off the line and it wasn't even funny. The beretta kept up for a while, and the grand prix was just toast off the line. Why is it I always get the middle finger and hardly ever the thumbs up?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||DecadenceR||06-07-2001||11:40 AM||||That wasn't the middle finger...<BR>That was his own personal way of telling you that you're number one!!!<P>*sigh*<BR>Some people... Just can't cope...<BR>I drive my 84 se on a 2 lane road to work every day (one lane north, one lane south) and there was this guy in a newer malibu behind me, riding my ass. Now, my car doesn't look fast. At this point it barely looks like a car. Anyway, I hit my brakes just enough to let the lights go on but not slow down. You see his car jerk back cause he slammed on his. Kinda funny. Now, i don't know how he expected me to go any faster since there was a large garbage truck in front of me. So at one point the opposing traffic stops, and this guy barrels past me and the truck on the left. Okay...<BR>So we get to the point of the road where the it goes to 2 lanes for maybe 1/3 of a mile. And who's at the light next to me? Yes sir, Mr Spanky himself. He gives me a dirty look, so I smile and put my foot on the gas and the brakes. Light hits green and i take off. I'm still half looking at him, and he's TRYING to keep up. His front bumper is about at my door, inching back... Inching back...<BR>By the point the road went back to just the 2 lanes again, he was about 4 car lenghts back. I thought I'd be nice and blink my tail lights at him to say hi. He gave me the <BR>"you're #1" sign. So nice of him.....  ;D||||reg||1
